@startuml M6-Data-Flow-Diagram

' Detailed data flow during indexing phase: raw repos -> extracted text -> tokens -> stemmed terms -> TF/DF calculation -> inverted index
' Shows all text processing steps: extract, normalize, tokenize, stem, n-grams
' Each step persists intermediate results and feeds into ranking calculations (TF-IDF, IDF weights)
' Final output: M4 distributed store persists inverted index, TF/DF stats, and IDF weights for search queries

!define BGCOLOR #F5F5F5
!define ACCENTCOLOR #1F77B4
!define ACCENTCOLOR2 #2CA02C
!define ACCENTCOLOR3 #FF7F0E

skinparam backgroundColor BGCOLOR
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #E8F4F8
skinparam activityBorderColor ACCENTCOLOR
skinparam activityFontColor #333
skinparam arrowColor #333

title M6 Search Engine - Data Flow Diagram (Indexing Phase)

(*) --> [Raw repository docs] activity RAW as "Raw Data\n{owner, repo, stars}"

RAW --> activity EXT as "Extract README\nMarkdown -> Text"

EXT --> activity NORM as "Normalize\nLowercase, Remove Punctuation"

NORM --> activity TOKEN as "Tokenize\nSplit into Words"

TOKEN --> activity STEM as "Stem\nPorter Stemmer"

STEM --> activity NGRAM as "Generate N-Grams\n1-gram, 2-gram, 3-gram"

NGRAM --> activity TF as "Calculate TF\nTerm Frequency per Doc"

TF --> activity DF as "Calculate DF\nDoc Frequency"

STEM --> activity IDX as "Build Inverted Index\nterm -> [docId, tf, ...]"

DF --> activity IDF as "Calculate IDF\nlog(N / df)"

TF --> IDX
IDX --> activity STORE as "M4 Store Writer\nSerialize -> Distribute"

IDF --> STORE

STORE --> [M4 Distributed Store\nIndex, TF, DF, IDF] (*)
